Description: avcodec/cbs_sei: delete the SEI unit when its last message is deleted
 Deleting the last message left a NAL unit containing only its header and
 trailing bits. CBS rejects that empty SEI, so a second bitstream filter
 could not read the output of h264_metadata=display_orientation=remove.
 Delete the unit when it has no messages left.
 .
 Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
 Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
 Assisted-by: gpt-6-astra via Codex
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, https://code.ffmpeg.org/danielcamposramos/FFmpeg/commit/3dd71847cf2c614d3a3b489ea146e5c8637ca5a3
Forwarded: https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/25395
Last-Update: 2026-11-06

diff --git a/libavcodec/cbs_sei.c b/libavcodec/cbs_sei.c
index e3544d3..70c18b4 100644
--- a/libavcodec/cbs_sei.c
+++ b/libavcodec/cbs_sei.c
@@ -582,6 +582,12 @@ void ff_cbs_sei_delete_message_type(CodedBitstreamContext *ctx,
             if (list->messages[j].payload_type == payload_type)
                 cbs_sei_delete_message(list, j);
         }
+
+        // An SEI unit needs at least one message.
+        if (!list->nb_messages) {
+            ff_cbs_delete_unit(au, i);
+            i--;
+        }
     }
 }
 
